<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Model Scoreboard — MFGA</title>
<style>
  /* Self-contained like admin/draft-sheet — desktop-first per Cory's doctrine,
     no JS. Tooltips are pure CSS hover with keyboard focus as the fallback. */
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { font-family: -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    color: #111; background: #fff; margin: 0; padding: 18px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.4; }
  h1 { font-size: 19px; margin: 0 0 2px; }
  h2 { font-size: 13px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .06em; margin: 20px 0 6px;
    border-bottom: 1.5px solid #111; padding-bottom: 3px; }
  .meta { font-size: 11.5px; color: #444; margin: 2px 0 8px; max-width: 74em; }
  .meta b, .card b { color: #111; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; margin: 4px 0 10px; }
  th, td { padding: 2.5px 8px; text-align: right; border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e2e2; white-space: nowrap; }
  th { font-size: 10.5px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .04em; color: #555;
    border-bottom: 1.5px solid #111; }
  td.nm, th.nm { text-align: left; }
  .champ { background: #f4f1e8; font-weight: 700; }      /* the live champion column */
  .prov  { background: #eef3f7; }                        /* provider study arms */
  .abs { color: #999; }
  .good { color: #0a6b2d; } .bad { color: #a01414; }
  .card { border: 1.5px solid #111; padding: 10px 12px; margin: 8px 0; max-width: 74em; }
  .ok { border-left: 5px solid #0a6b2d; }
  .warn { border-left: 5px solid #b06d00; }
  .confirm { background: #eaf6ec; border: 1px solid #0a6b2d; color: #0a4d20;
    padding: 6px 10px; font-size: 12px; margin: 8px 0; max-width: 74em; }
  form.src label { display: inline-block; margin: 3px 14px 3px 0; font-weight: 600; }
  form.src button { font-weight: 700; padding: 3px 12px; margin-left: 6px; }
  code { background: #f4f4f4; padding: 0 3px; font-size: 11.5px; }
  /* ⓘ tooltips: hover on desktop, focus (tab / tap on the symbol) as fallback. */
  .info { position: relative; display: inline-block; cursor: help; color: #1a5276;
    font-weight: 700; margin-left: 3px; outline: none; }
  .info .tip { display: none; position: absolute; z-index: 9; left: 0; top: 1.4em;
    width: 26em; max-width: 70vw; background: #111; color: #fff; font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 11.5px; line-height: 1.45; padding: 8px 10px; border-radius: 3px;
    white-space: normal; text-align: left; text-transform: none; letter-spacing: 0; }
  .info:hover .tip, .info:focus .tip { display: block; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Model scoreboard &amp; controls</h1>
<p class="meta">
  Every number on this page IS the weekly learning ledger's number
  (<code>draft/data/weekly_own/grades_<%= season %>.json</code>, written by the
  Tuesday grade cron) — nothing is recomputed here. Our Thursday snapshot prices
  every QB/RB/WR/TE <b>before kickoff</b>; the Tuesday grade scores every arm
  against what actually happened, on the same players.
  <span class="info" tabindex="0">&#9432;<span class="tip">WHAT: our own weekly
  projection model plus its challenger variants and the provider study arms
  (Sleeper, FantasyPros, their average), graded weekly on identical players.
  READ: lower MAE = closer to what happened; higher rank correlation = better
  ordering. DO: nothing is required — the loop adapts itself and opens a GitHub
  issue (which emails you) whenever the champion changes.</span></span>
</p>

<% if (saved && saved !== 'invalid') { %>
  <p class="confirm">Saved. The in-season projection feed
  (<code>src/proj_feed.js</code>) now derives its season-rate from
  <b><%= saved %></b> — every surface that reads the feed changes together on
  its next render. This switch does <b>not</b> touch the draft board.</p>
<% } else if (saved === 'invalid') { %>
  <p class="confirm" style="background:#fbeeee;border-color:#a01414;color:#5a0d0d">
  Not saved — that was not one of the known sources.</p>
<% } %>

<h2>Champion &amp; adaptation</h2>
<div class="card <%= controls.champion_override ? 'warn' : 'ok' %>">
  Current champion: <b><%= champion.version %></b> (arm <code><%= champion.arm %></code>)
  <span class="info" tabindex="0">&#9432;<span class="tip">WHAT: the arm whose
  number is the "our model" column everywhere. Its formula:
  <%= (activeArms.find(a => a.name === champion.arm) || {}).formula || 'proj_ownmodel/17 with the vegas tilt (see README)' %>.
  READ: the version bumps (v1 → v2 …) every time the champion changes, so
  grades are never silently mixed across formulas. DO: normally nothing — the
  Tuesday rule promotes the best challenger mechanically.</span></span>
  <br>Auto-adaptation:
  <% if (controls.champion_override) { %>
    <b>PAUSED by manual override</b> — champion column pinned to
    <code><%= controls.champion_override %></code> via
    <code>draft/data/weekly_own/controls.json</code>.
  <% } else if (controls.auto_adapt) { %>
    <b>ON</b> — a challenger is promoted when it has ≥3 graded weeks, beat the
    champion in ≥3 of the last 4, leads cumulative MAE, and gives up no more
    than 0.02 rank correlation. Earliest possible switch: after week 3.
  <% } else { %>
    <b>PAUSED</b> (<code>auto_adapt: false</code> in
    <code>draft/data/weekly_own/controls.json</code>) — grading continues,
    promotions held.
  <% } %>
  <span class="info" tabindex="0">&#9432;<span class="tip">WHAT: whether the
  Tuesday grader may switch champions on its own (your ruling: adapt often —
  this data is not used for decisions in 2026, so a wrong switch costs
  nothing and reverses itself). READ: every switch, mechanical or manual,
  lands in the history below AND opens a GitHub issue that emails you. DO:
  to pause adaptation or pin an arm by hand, edit
  <code>draft/data/weekly_own/controls.json</code> in the repo (ask any
  session) — a site button for this needs a bridge from the site to the CI
  grader and is honestly not wired yet, so no button is shown.</span></span>
</div>

<h2>Live-tools projection source</h2>
<p class="meta">
  Which numbers the in-season surfaces (lineup / waivers / matchup gap) derive
  their per-player weekly rate from. All options are the board's season totals
  ÷ 17 — a <b>level, not a weekly forecast</b> — scored under our own table at
  build time. The weekly ledger above is exactly the evidence for flipping
  this: the <code>sleeper</code> / <code>fantasypros</code> /
  <code>sleeper_fp_average</code> study arms answer "who is winning, and does
  averaging beat both."
  <span class="info" tabindex="0">&#9432;<span class="tip">WHAT: a real switch —
  it writes the <code>model_controls</code> doc, and
  <code>src/proj_feed.js</code> (the one shared feed) reads it; nothing else
  does. READ: <b>blend</b> = proj_mean, the Sleeper+FP blend the tools have
  always used (default = current behavior). <b>sleeper</b> / <b>fantasypros</b>
  = that provider's season total alone. <b>sleeper_fp_average</b> = their
  simple mean (when one side is missing a player, the feed uses the other and
  says so in its basis string — never a silent zero). DO: read the cumulative
  table first; switch only when an arm is clearly winning over several
  weeks.</span></span>
</p>
<form class="src" method="post" action="/admin/model-scoreboard/source">
  <% for (const s of sources) { %>
    <label><input type="radio" name="source" value="<%= s %>"
      <%= s === source ? 'checked' : '' %>> <%= s %><%= s === 'blend' ? ' (default)' : '' %></label>
  <% } %>
  <button type="submit">Set source</button>
  <span class="meta">now: <b><%= source %></b></span>
</form>
<p class="meta">
  Deliberately <b>not</b> a control here: the draft board's <code>proj_mean</code>
  composition — evidence-blocked until the January 2027 grade of the frozen 2026
  archive (REC-2) — and scoring weights, ever.
</p>

<% if (!weeks.length) { %>
  <h2>Scoreboard</h2>
  <div class="card">No grades yet — the first own-weekly snapshot commits
  Thursday <b>Sep 10</b> (before kickoff) and the first real grades land
  <b>~Sep 15</b>. Nothing is shown until then because nothing has been
  measured; this page never fakes a row.</div>
<% } else { %>

<h2>Cumulative scoreboard <span class="info" tabindex="0">&#9432;<span class="tip">
  WHAT: each arm's average weekly MAE (mean absolute error, points per player)
  and rank correlation across all graded weeks. Provider rows are computed on
  the players shared with our arms, so every row prices the same people.
  READ: lowest MAE wins; correlation above ~0.5 means the ordering is real.
  DO: this table is what the promotion rule reads — and your evidence for the
  source switch above.</span></span></h2>
<table>
  <tr><th class="nm">arm</th><th>kind</th><th>weeks</th><th>MAE</th><th>rank corr</th></tr>
  <% for (const arm of armNames.concat(provNames)) { const c = cum[arm]; if (!c) continue; %>
  <tr class="<%= arm === champion.arm ? 'champ' : (c.kind === 'provider' ? 'prov' : '') %>">
    <td class="nm"><%= arm %><%= arm === champion.arm ? ' ← champion' : '' %></td>
    <td><%= c.kind === 'provider' ? 'study (never auto-promoted)' : 'ours' %></td>
    <td><%= c.weeks %></td>
    <td><%= c.mae == null ? '—' : c.mae %></td>
    <td><%= c.spearman == null ? '—' : c.spearman %></td>
  </tr>
  <% } %>
</table>

<h2>Week by week (MAE) <span class="info" tabindex="0">&#9432;<span class="tip">
  WHAT: each graded week's mean absolute error per arm — ours on the full
  graded population, providers on the shared players. READ: a challenger that
  beats the champion 3 of the last 4 weeks (and leads cumulative) gets
  promoted automatically. DO: look for streaks, not single weeks — one week
  is mostly noise.</span></span></h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>week</th>
    <% for (const arm of armNames) { %><th><%= arm %></th><% } %>
    <% for (const arm of provNames) { %><th><%= arm %></th><% } %>
    <th class="nm">graded / projected</th></tr>
  <% for (const w of weeks) { %>
  <tr>
    <td><%= w.week %></td>
    <% for (const arm of armNames) { const c = w.own[arm]; %>
      <td class="<%= arm === w.champion_arm ? 'champ' : '' %>"><%= c && c.mae != null ? c.mae : '—' %></td>
    <% } %>
    <% for (const arm of provNames) { const c = (w.prov[arm] || {}).shared; %>
      <td class="prov"><%= c && c.mae != null ? c.mae : '—' %></td>
    <% } %>
    <td class="nm"><%= w.population.with_actual %> / <%= w.population.projected %>
      <span class="info" tabindex="0">&#9432;<span class="tip">
      <%= w.population.no_stat_row.count %> projected player(s) had no stat row
      this week (inactive/injured) — they are counted here and excluded from
      the error math, never scored as zero. Champion that week:
      <%= w.champion_arm %> under <%= w.formula %>.</span></span></td>
  </tr>
  <% } %>
</table>

<% if (latest) { %>
<h2>Biggest misses — week <%= latest.week %> <span class="info" tabindex="0">&#9432;<span class="tip">
  WHAT: the champion arm's five largest absolute errors last week, by name.
  err &gt; 0 = we projected points that never came (over); err &lt; 0 = a real
  blow-up we missed (under). READ: this is WHY the model was wrong, in
  players, not just a number. DO: patterns here are where new challenger arms
  come from.</span></span></h2>
<p class="meta"><%= latest.miss_pattern %></p>
<table>
  <tr><th class="nm">player</th><th>pos</th><th>proj</th><th>actual</th><th>err</th></tr>
  <% for (const m of latest.top_misses) { %>
  <tr>
    <td class="nm"><%= m.name || m.player_id %></td>
    <td><%= m.pos || '—' %></td>
    <td><%= m.proj %></td>
    <td><%= m.actual %></td>
    <td class="<%= m.err > 0 ? 'bad' : 'good' %>"><%= m.err > 0 ? '+' : '' %><%= m.err %></td>
  </tr>
  <% } %>
</table>
<% } %>
<% } %>

<h2>Adaptation history <span class="info" tabindex="0">&#9432;<span class="tip">
  WHAT: every champion change — mechanical promotions and manual overrides —
  with the evidence it rode in on. Each one also opened a GitHub issue that
  emailed you. READ: the version string tells you which formula produced any
  week's numbers; nothing is ever silently mixed.</span></span></h2>
<% if (!promotions.length) { %>
  <p class="meta">None yet — the champion is still <b><%= champion.version %></b>
  (arm <code><%= champion.arm %></code>). The earliest possible mechanical
  switch is after three graded weeks (~early October).</p>
<% } else { %>
<table>
  <tr><th>when</th><th class="nm">what</th><th class="nm">evidence</th></tr>
  <% for (const p of promotions) { %>
  <tr>
    <td><%= p.promoted_at %></td>
    <td class="nm"><%= p.type === 'manual_override' ? 'manual override' : 'mechanical promotion' %>:
      <%= (p.from || {}).arm %> → <b><%= (p.to || {}).arm %></b>
      (<%= (p.to || {}).version %>)</td>
    <td class="nm"><% if (p.evidence) { %>won <%= p.evidence.recent_wins %>,
      cum MAE <%= p.evidence.cum_mae %> vs <%= p.evidence.champion_cum_mae %>
      over weeks <%= (p.evidence.weeks_used || []).join(', ') %><% } else { %>
      <%= p.note || '—' %><% } %></td>
  </tr>
  <% } %>
</table>
<% } %>

<p class="meta">
  Loop contract, formulas and the verbatim promotion rule:
  <code>draft/data/weekly_own/README.md</code>. Provider arms are STUDY arms —
  graded, never auto-promoted; which provider feeds the live tools is the
  switch above and stays your call.
</p>
</body>
</html>
